{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"id":"PR_kwDOQ7Tfmc7GZoba","reviewThreads":{"nodes":[{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08P1","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455086,"body":"This endpoint currently returns `{ success, note, task }` (see `packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts`), not a top-level task object. Asserting `updatedTask.notes` here will fail against the implemented API and doesn't validate the actual contract."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08P2","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455087,"body":"Same response-shape issue here: `response.json()` for `POST /note` is wrapped (`{ success, note, task }`). This test should read from `body.note` and/or `body.task.notes` instead of assuming a top-level `notes` array."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08P6","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455092,"body":"This can pass vacuously if the API returns an empty `items` array. That matters here because the current route implementation does not split comma-separated status values, so this test may report success without actually verifying comma-separated filter support. Add a non-empty assertion (or compare against the multi-value query result)."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08P7","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455093,"body":"The fallback 409 branch weakens this test and is based on an incorrect isolation assumption. The `daemon` fixture in `test-base.ts` is test-scoped (no worker scope configured), so this test should start from a fresh fixture and require `200` here; otherwise a broken `/start` implementation can still pass this test."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08P_","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455096,"body":"Please verify this against actual daemon behavior: the route declares `body: t.Object({ content: t.String() })`, so Elysia may reject `{}` before the handler's custom `validation_error` response runs. This test may be asserting the wrong status/body shape for the real endpoint."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08QB","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455102,"body":"This test becomes a no-op if no item includes `spec_ref`, which means it can pass even if the list endpoint stops returning `spec_ref` entirely. Since the fixtures include tasks with `spec_ref`, assert that a matching task exists before validating the field."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5w08QE","isResolved":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":2856455106,"body":"The test name says 'ULID prefix', but this sends the full ULID. Either use a unique prefix (to exercise prefix resolution) or rename the test to exact ULID resolution."}]}}]}}}}}
